Chíun (Silent Night)</strong>”: a re-recorded version of the Enya Christmas classic, in Gaelic.
Enya says that “It was exciting to re-live ‘Silent
Night’ because I sung that
twenty years ago. It is re-released every year in America and it was so
nice to go back and do something different with it.” The new
rendering incorporates
what Nicky describes as the “choir of one”,
multi-layering Enya vocals. “I
enjoy the process, I love the excitement of not knowing if it will
work,” admits Enya.</li>
<li>And we can count that, like in all past Enya albums, “<strong>And Winter Came...</strong>” may be a song title
as well. Warner also said that the album comprises 12 songs, 10 in English and none instrumental (the first Enya album without them!).</li></ul>
<p>Roma also talks about the title and the “sense of possibility that Christmas
brings”: “some
people see it <em>[the winter]</em> as an ending, with a
whole story before it, but
I see it very much as a new beginning.”</p>
<p>More
specific release dates were also disclosed:</p>
<ul><li>US:
November
11th (by Amazon.com)</li>
<li>Japan:
November
12th (by Warner Music Japan)</li></ul>
<p>Finally,

<a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/redirect.html?ie=UTF8&location=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2F2008-Release-Enya%2Fdp%2FB001EI5CA0&tag=enylyrallenys-20&linkCode=ur2&camp=1789&creative=9325">a
bigger cover image</a> was released by Amazon.com, though we still
don’t know what
the “7” in the lower right stands for.</p>
