<h4>OFFICIAL: Winter coming earlier for Enya fans!</h4>

<p><strong class="date">September 15 2008 —</strong> Enya
just announced in her revamped official website that her new album, <em><a href="/and-winter-came/">And Winter Came...</a></em> (<a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/redirect.html?ie=UTF8&location=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.amazon.com%2F2008-Release-Enya%2Fdp%2FB001EI5CA0&tag=enylyrallenys-20&linkCode=ur2&camp=1789&creative=9325">pre-order on Amazon.com</a>), will be released on November 10<sup>th</sup>. Enya says
that she “always wanted to do a Christmas album, but as we began recording I didn't feel it was right to impose a Christmas theme on certain  songs.”</p>

<a href="/and-winter-came/"><Image src={newalbum} style="float:left; margin:0 20px 10px 0;" alt="Enya new album cover"  width="150" height="150" /></a>
<p>The album cover was also revealed, though in a small size.</p>
<p><a href="/roma-ryan-nicky/">Nicky Ryan</a>, her producer since <a href="/enya-album/">the first album</a>, adds that they “started out writing for a
Christmas album, but it has evolved into more an Enya album based in a
winter landscape where Christmas arrives here and there, but it would be wrong to call it an Enya Christmas album.”</p>
