<h3>July 2008</h3>

<h4>Top 10 Enya songs (Part 7) — Article</h4>

<p><strong class="date">July 11 2008 —</strong> After one month on
vacations, we’re ready to continue our list of best Enya
Songs, this time with a Latin piece.</p>

<Image src={afad} alt="Enya Lyrics"  width="150" height="150" />

<h5><strong>#4 “Afer Ventus”</strong>, from 1991’s album <a href="/shepherd-moons/">Shepherd Moons</a></h5>

<p>According to Enya’s right arm, Roma Ryan, who writes nearly all her songs, “Afer Ventus” talks about the <em>Epiphany</em>, that magical moment of “revelation” and comprehension of the world gears. “The moment experienced when everything in life suddenly makes sense—when everything fits into place and we know why—is a rare moment, but it does
 appen”, she adds in <a href="/shepherd-moons/#linearnotes"><em>Shepherd Moons</em> linear notes</a>. “If we are lucky enough we can bathe in the brevity of that moment for it passes as quickly as it arrives. Like [James] Joyce’s <em>Epiphanies</em> they can sometimes seem trivial, but are always crucial and revealing moments in our lives, delicate and fleeting. In ‘Afer Ventus’ it is those moments of pure enlightenment which are  described”.</p>
<p>“Afer Ventus” is surely a calm, reflexive song. Enya calls winds, seas, stars and planets to tell a history of self-knowledge and to advise the listener that the life is short,
unique and is “earth-born” even if “we go to the
stars”, that is, life should be lived intensely,
but with care at the same time. Latin, as a ancient language, adds
weight and profoundness to the song, like it was indeed an ancient history.</p>
<p>Of course, you don’t have to agree
with my humble interpretation: just <a href="mailto:orangax@gmail.com">send me an email</a> saying what you
think about “Afer Ventus” and/or your own top ten Enya
songs. I’ll be very glad to hear you and to publish your opinions here.</p>
<p>Thanks for reading! And please, keep
enjoying Enya Lyrics.</p>

<p><strong><small><em>by</em> <a href="http://flipdarius.googlepages.com/">Felipe Dário</a>, Enya Lyrics webmaster</small></strong></p>

