<h3>March 2008</h3>
<h4>Top 10 Enya songs (Part 2) — Article</h4>
<p><strong class="date">March 30 2008 —</strong>  continuing our list of <strong>best Enya songs</strong>, we have now...</p>
<h5><strong>#9 “<a href="/the-memory-of-trees/">The Memory of Trees</a>”</strong>, from the 1995’s <a href="/the-memory-of-trees/">eponymous album</a>.</h5>
<p>According to <a href="/roma-ryan-nicky/">Roma Ryan</a>, who writes all Enya songs, “In ancient Celtic belief trees had spirits within them and were considered sacred. They were the keepers of memory and lore.” This is an instrumental song, with Enya’s classical one-voice chorus singing understandable words that convey tranquility. The perceived passivity of the trees (the piano) is put together with the powerful and mysterious chants of “biondella”, that may be blow by the wind through the leaves and branches.</p>
<p>I still want to hear you: which is
your Enya top ten songs? And what you think about “The Memory of Trees”? Email me: <a href="mailto:orangax@gmail.com&subject=Enya%20Lyrics%20-%20Top%20ten%20Enya%20songs">orangax@gmail.com</a>. Your opinion will be published here.</p>
