<h4>Top 10 Enya songs (Part 1) — Article</h4>
<p><strong class="date">March 25 2008 —</strong> Selecting Enya best songs isn’t an easy work. Her albums made into the bestsellers world
wide, with so many beautiful songs. She sometimes calm us down
(“<a href="/enya-other/#Adeste_Fideles">Adeste, Fidelis</a>”), sometimes make us cry (“<a href="/a-day-without-rain/#Only_Time">Only Time</a>”), and surely cause many more feelings.</p>
<p>But, as any fan, I have my personal favorites, and
I’d like to share them with you. Starting from now,
I’ll rank the <strong>10 Best Enya songs</strong>, one per week, followed by a small analysis.</p>
<h5><strong>#10 “<a href="/the-memory-of-trees/#Anywhere_Is">Anywhere Is</a>”</strong>, from 1995’s <a href="/the-memory-of-trees/"><em>The Memory Of Trees</em></a>.</h5>
<p>Enya talks about the need to always keep going. Like the moon
and sea waves, that never stops, even without knowing why, we either
should stop. This is the circle of life: there’s not really a finish. And our way may lead us to everywhere we want to. After all,
it’s made by us, isn’t it? And the song per se is beautiful and compelling, with a <em>fake
end</em>—again, Enya says “keep going”.</p>
<p>Well, of course this is my personal interpretation and opinion, you
don’t have to agree. But I would love to hear you: which is
